---
// "What it is" — sets the side-car mental model before the detailed pipeline.
---

<section class="sidecar section" id="sidecar">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it fits</p>
    <h2 class="section-title sidecar__title">
      It doesn&rsquo;t replace paperless-ngx.<br />It works for it.
    </h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Run it as a second container beside your stack. It talks to paperless over the same
      REST API you already use — reading the documents you tag, writing back metadata, and
      removing the tag when it&rsquo;s done. Nothing else in your archive changes.
    </p>

    <ul class="principles">
      <li class="principles__item">
        <span class="principles__k">beside, not instead</span>
        <p>
          A separate container that speaks paperless&rsquo;s API. Your library, tags and
          workflow stay exactly as they are.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="principles__item">
        <span class="principles__k">one tag, in your hands</span>
        <p>
          Tag a document <code>psf-process</code> and it gets picked up. Re-tag to reprocess.
          Leave it untagged and it&rsquo;s never touched.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="principles__item">
        <span class="principles__k">your call to apply</span>
        <p>
          Write changes straight back, or hold every suggestion in a review queue until you
          approve it — a single setting.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .sidecar {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    background: var(--paper-2);
  }

  .sidecar__title {
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .principles {
    list-style: none;
    margin: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 28px;
  }

  .principles__item {
    padding-top: 18px;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .principles__k {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rind-deep);
  }

  .principles__item p {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .principles code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    background: var(--gold-tint);
    border: 1px solid var(--gold-soft);
    color: var(--gold-deep);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .principles {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }
</style>
